+**Two files predate the guide, on purpose.** Both are scripted
+`podTemplate`/`node` files, so neither is a model for a new file: a new file
+starts from its type's reference file. How to treat each:
+
+- ModernAppTemplate's own template, `root/template/Jenkinsfile.jinja`. It is
+  brought to the guide at the template's next sync, when an agent reconciles the
+  template with the apps it renders: DHCPApp, ElectronicsInventory,
+  FieldnotesApp, IoTSupport and ZigbeeControl, whose `Jenkinsfile` are on the
+  guide's
+  [modern app build](https://pipelines.home/docs/types/modern-app/index.md)
+  type. Until that sync, an app rendered from the template does not build: the
+  file calls `containerTemplates.k8s` and the positional `helmCharts.kaniko(…)`,
+  which the library no longer has.
+- KitchenDisplay's `Jenkinsfile`, the job `Firmware/KitchenDisplay`. The job is
+  disabled, and the file waits with it for the decision on the display's future
+  (ANS-93, parked). Leave it as it is. The library keeps the code it calls:
+  `containerTemplates.rsync` and `dockbuild`, `helmCharts.ssh` and `rsync`, and
+  `gitUtils`. Its `Jenkinsfile.architecture` is on the guide.
+
